---
---

<section id="split" class="py-24 sm:py-36 max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 sm:px-10">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12 lg:gap-16 items-center">
    
    <!-- Text Column -->
    <div class="lg:col-span-5 space-y-6">
      <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-idle-green">
        03 / Split View
      </span>
      <h2 class="text-4xl sm:text-6xl md:text-7xl font-bold tracking-tight text-charcoal leading-[1.05]">
        Stop playing <br/>
        <span class="font-serif italic font-normal text-idle-green">tab tennis.</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-lg sm:text-xl text-charcoal-muted leading-relaxed font-normal pt-2">
        <p>
          Researching something while writing? Comparing two products? Following a tutorial while pretending you know what you're doing?
        </p>
        <p>
          Constantly switching between tabs gets old.
        </p>
        <p class="font-medium text-charcoal">
          Idle lets you put pages side by side, so you can see everything at once.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Sub-features -->
      <div class="space-y-6 pt-4 border-t border-charcoal-border-subtle">
        <div class="space-y-1">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-charcoal">Drag to split</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-charcoal-muted leading-relaxed">
            Drag a tab into the page to open it alongside another. No resizing windows or rearranging your desktop.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-1">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-charcoal">Your space, your rules</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-charcoal-muted leading-relaxed">
            Go 50/50, 70/30, or whatever works. Just drag the divider.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-1">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-charcoal">Room for more</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-charcoal-muted leading-relaxed">
            Need a little extra? Split up to four panes, horizontally or vertically.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Tagline -->
      <p class="pt-2 text-sm font-serif italic text-idle-green font-medium">
        Less switching. More doing.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Authentic Side-by-Side Visual Mockup -->
    <div class="lg:col-span-7">
      <div class="rounded-3xl p-3 bg-charcoal shadow-2xl border border-charcoal/20">
        <!-- Window titlebar mockup -->
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-3 py-2 text-xs text-warm-bg/40 font-mono">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-white/20"></span>
            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-white/20"></span>
            <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-white/20"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="text-[11px] text-warm-bg/60">Idle · Split View (2 Panes)</div>
          <div class="w-8"></div>
        </div>

        <!-- Split Canvas Container -->
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-2 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden bg-[#181918] p-2 text-warm-bg">
          <!-- Left Pane -->
          <div class="rounded-xl bg-[#222422] p-6 sm:p-7 border border-white/5 space-y-4">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-warm-bg/50 pb-2 border-b border-white/5">
              <span class="truncate font-mono">nature.org/deep-sea-bioluminescence</span>
              <span class="text-idle-green-light shrink-0">Pane 1</span>
            </div>
            <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-warm-bg leading-snug">
              Bioluminescence in the Abyssal Twilight
            </h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-warm-bg/70 leading-relaxed font-sans">
              Organisms living below 1,000 meters produce their own cold light using luciferin-luciferase reactions. In utter darkness, flashing patterns serve as both camouflage and communication.
            </p>
            <div class="pt-2 text-[11px] text-warm-bg/40 font-mono">
              Reference tab · 100% zoom
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Right Pane -->
          <div class="rounded-xl bg-[#222422] p-6 sm:p-7 border border-white/5 space-y-4">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-xs text-warm-bg/50 pb-2 border-b border-white/5">
              <span class="truncate font-mono">notes.local/ocean-chapter-4</span>
              <span class="text-idle-green-light shrink-0">Pane 2</span>
            </div>
            <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-warm-bg leading-snug">
              Drafting: Marine Optics & Sensors
            </h4>
            <p class="text-xs text-warm-bg/70 leading-relaxed font-sans">
              Key takeaway for Section 4: We can tune sensor thresholds to match the spectral peak (~470 nm) observed in deep-sea photophores, drastically lowering false positives in twilight surveys.
            </p>
            <div class="pt-2 text-[11px] text-idle-green-light font-mono flex items-center gap-1.5">
              <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-idle-green-light animate-pulse"></span>
              Live editing alongside reference
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Split status hint -->
        <div class="py-2.5 px-3 text-center text-[11px] text-warm-bg/40 font-mono">
          Drag divider to adjust ratio (50/50, 70/30) · Press <kbd class="px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded bg-white/10 text-warm-bg">⌘W</kbd> to close active pane
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
